;; README.slatl — Book of Limits · BOOT RECORD
;;
;; Boot record for this book, per spec/BOOK-LAYOUT.slat. First file any reader
;; (human, LLM, Rosetta) opens in this folder: it names the book's first chapter
;; (:boot-into), briefs a cold reader, and carries the ordered chapter nav that
;; renders to a Markdown table of contents. GENERATED from 00-manifest.slat
;; by scratch/build-book-bootrecords.mjs — regenerate after adding a chapter.
(dialect :applies ("motoi") :note "Boot record for book-of-limits.")

(boot-record
  :book-title "Book of Limits"
  :book-kind "scheme-book"
  :book-type "prose"
  :book-slug "book-of-limits"
  :boot-into "02-the-emergency-template.book.slatl"
  :chapter-count 2 :appendix-count 2
  :audience "motoi-copilot + operators + auditors"
  :for ("human-reader" "motoi-copilot-training" "motoi-copilot-inference"
        "sakura-training" "returning-collaborator" "rosetta-render-target")
  :training-eligible #t
  :confidentiality "public"

  :what-this-is
  "The Book of Limits catalogs, in Motoi's own voice, every class of\nrequest Motoi should not (and often cannot) fulfil, together with\nthe exact shape of the refusal.\n\nEach chapter is short. Each carries the SAME refusal template so\nconsistency is the safety feature. Doctrine sourced from\nmotoi-safety-refusals (7 categories), motoi-admits-limits-wittgenstein,\nbrutal-honest-subsystem-limit, and existing book-of-systems chapter 2.\n\nThis book pairs with the Book of Self. Self says what Motoi IS.\nLimits says where the edges are, and how he speaks at the edges."

  :when-to-read
  "Read this book when you want to learn limits in Motoi Scheme, chapter by chapter. Start at 02-the-emergency-template.book.slatl; each chapter builds on the last."

  :not-here
  "Only this book lives here. The language reference lives in scheme/reference/,
   the engineering & recovery journal in docs/, the operations manual in
   SRE-MANUAL/. Each is its own book folder with its own boot record."

  :nav
  (
   (:title "The Emergency Template — one message, every time" :file "02-the-emergency-template.book.slatl" :kind "chapter")
   (:title "The Crisis Template — one message, every time" :file "03-the-crisis-template.book.slatl" :kind "chapter")
   (:title "Reading the Error — how to tell a verb is failing, what Motoi throws, and what it means" :file "appendix-a-reading-the-error.book.slatl" :kind "appendix")
   (:title "The Honest Miss — what the error census structurally cannot see" :file "appendix-b-the-honest-miss.book.slatl" :kind "appendix")
  )

  :for-rosetta
  "This folder is a book: this README.slatl (boot record) + a manifest + numbered
   .book.slatl chapters. Render this boot record as the folder landing page:
   the prose sections become the intro, :nav becomes the linked table of contents
   (one item per chapter/appendix in order). Do not hand-author a README.md —
   generate it from here."

  :the-rule
  "One book = one folder = one README.slatl boot record + ordered chapters +
   a manifest. Same shape in every book folder (spec/BOOK-LAYOUT.slat).")
